sequenceDiagram
    autonumber

    actor Admin as Administrator
    participant UI as Web Portal
    participant BatchAPI as BatchDiscountsController
    participant Promotion as PromotionService
    participant PromoStore as PromotionStore
    participant RuleAPI as ShelfLifeDiscountsController
    participant RuleService as ShelfLifeDiscountService
    participant RuleStore as ShelfLifeDiscountStore
    participant DB as PostgreSQL Database

    %% ==========================================
    %% 1. SCAN NEAR-EXPIRY BATCHES
    %% ==========================================

    Admin->>+UI: Open Shelf-Life Discount Management

    UI->>+BatchAPI: Suggestions(filters)
    BatchAPI->>+Promotion: ListBatchSuggestionsAsync(filters)

    Promotion->>+PromoStore: ListBatchDiscountCandidatesAsync(filters)
    PromoStore->>+DB: SELECT eligible batches, expiry dates and stock balances
    DB-->>PromoStore: Batch and inventory records
    deactivate DB

    PromoStore-->>Promotion: Candidate batch list
    deactivate PromoStore

    Promotion-->>BatchAPI: Batch discount suggestions
    deactivate Promotion

    BatchAPI-->>UI: Candidate batch results
    deactivate BatchAPI

    %% ==========================================
    %% 2. VIEW CURRENT DISCOUNT CONFIGURATION
    %% ==========================================

    UI->>+RuleAPI: Current()
    RuleAPI->>+RuleService: GetCurrentAsync()

    RuleService->>+RuleStore: FindCurrentAsync()
    RuleStore->>+DB: SELECT current discount table and tiers
    DB-->>RuleStore: Active configuration
    deactivate DB

    RuleStore-->>RuleService: Current discount table
    deactivate RuleStore

    RuleService-->>RuleAPI: Current discount configuration
    deactivate RuleService

    RuleAPI-->>UI: Discount rules response
    deactivate RuleAPI

    UI-->>Admin: Display near-expiry batches and current rules
    deactivate UI

    %% ==========================================
    %% 3. CONFIGURE SHELF-LIFE DISCOUNT RULES
    %% ==========================================

    opt Administrator creates or updates discount configuration

        Admin->>+UI: Enter discount tiers and effective period

        Note over Admin,UI: Configure Category or SKU, remaining-life range and discount percentage

        UI->>+RuleAPI: Publish(discountTableData)
        RuleAPI->>+RuleService: PublishAsync(discountTableData)

        Note right of RuleService: Validate target, percentage and non-overlapping ranges

        RuleService->>+RuleStore: FindCurrentForUpdateAsync()
        RuleStore->>+DB: SELECT current configuration and version
        DB-->>RuleStore: Current table and tiers
        deactivate DB

        RuleStore-->>RuleService: Existing configuration
        deactivate RuleStore

        alt Valid configuration and no version conflict

            RuleService->>+RuleStore: MaxVersionAsync()
            RuleStore->>+DB: SELECT latest discount table version
            DB-->>RuleStore: Latest version number
            deactivate DB

            RuleStore-->>RuleService: Version information
            deactivate RuleStore

            RuleService->>+RuleStore: AddTable(), AddTiers(), SaveChangesAsync()

            RuleStore->>+DB: INSERT new discount table, tiers and audit record
            DB-->>RuleStore: Configuration committed
            deactivate DB

            RuleStore-->>RuleService: Published discount version
            deactivate RuleStore

        else Invalid discount rules or conflicting version

            Note right of RuleService: Reject overlapping ranges, invalid percentages or conflicting updates

        end

        RuleService-->>RuleAPI: Published configuration or business error
        deactivate RuleService

        RuleAPI-->>UI: Publication response
        deactivate RuleAPI

        UI-->>Admin: Display published rules or validation errors
        deactivate UI

    end

    Note over RuleService,DB: Published rules are applied during allocation pricing after MLOR filtering